<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* UI-001: Office White is a DevExpress *Classic* theme -- Classic themes bundle Bootstrap CSS, so one
       theme styles BOTH the DevExpress components AND the app's own Bootstrap-classed chrome cohesively.
       Fluent (the previous theme) is Design-System-based and does NOT style native HTML/Bootstrap chrome,
       which left the surrounding app bare -> the "very minimal styling" the owner saw. Because the Classic
       theme provides Bootstrap, the standalone bootstrap.min.css link is dropped (loading both double-loads
       and conflicts). RegisterTheme (over raw links) manages the CSS cache across DX versions. Verified via
       dxdocs 401523 (26.1). To try another look it's a one-liner: Themes.BlazingBerry / .Purple / .BlazingDark. *@
    @DxResourceManager.RegisterTheme(Themes.OfficeWhite)
    @DxResourceManager.RegisterScripts()
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    @* Modernist design system (design_handoff_modernist_xaf). Loads LAST on purpose: it overrides
       both the Classic theme's Bootstrap layer and app.css's chrome, and equal-specificity rules are
       won by whoever comes last. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["modernist-theme.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveAuto" />
</head>

<body>
    @* Global InteractiveAuto: the router (and the whole RCL page tree) runs Server-side on the first
       visit, then WebAssembly once the runtime is cached. Routes lives in the RCL. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveAuto" />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
